# Sparse runoff package parameters (pkg/rnf)
#
# The same runoff as the dense case input.rnof_daily, in sparse form:
# 40 daily records from 1 January 1979 00:00, not repeated:
# the file says mitgcm_time_sampling = "fixed",
# mitgcm_time_period = 86400 and mitgcm_time_repeat = "none".
#
# The file is written by ../input.rnof_const/gen_sparse.py from the
# dense records of input.rnof_daily and is read from that directory,
# so both cases force the model with the same runoff. Every timing
# value the reader needs comes from the file's own time axis, which is
# what this case checks; data.rnf overrides nothing.
#
# RNF_debugLev = 3 (debLevC) makes RNF_FIELDS_LOAD print, at every step,
# the two records it bracketed, the file year of each and the weight of
# the earlier one. That trace is what the sparse timing check reads from
# this run directory (tests/runoff/lab_sea_runoff_timing_check.py); it
# only prints and changes no value.
 &RNF_PARM01
  RNF_file = '../input.rnof_daily/runoff_sparse.nc',
  RNF_debugLev = 3,
 &
